DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Helsinki:20261027T130000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Helsinki:20261027T140000
SUMMARY:AiLIFE: Olli Kallioniemi — Towards AI-Native Molecular Medicine
  Research: A Life Scientist's Perspective
LOCATION:Biomedicum Helsinki 1\, Seminar rooms 1–2\, Haartmaninkatu 8\,
  00290 Helsinki
DESCRIPTION:AiLIFE: Accelerating Life Sciences with AI and Agents\nRegist
 ration: https://elomake.helsinki.fi/lomakkeet/141857/lomake.html
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-11-24@ailife.helsinki
DTSTAMP:20261022T103812Z
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Helsinki:20261124T130000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Helsinki:20261124T140000
SUMMARY:AiLIFE: Esa Pitkänen — AI Agents for Life Sciences: From Ad Ho
 c Software to Automated Computational Method Development
LOCATION:Biomedicum Helsinki 1\, Seminar room 3\, Haartmaninkatu 8\, 0029
 0 Helsinki
DESCRIPTION:AiLIFE: Accelerating Life Sciences with AI and Agents\n\nMode
 rn AI agents are language models that pursue a goal by repeatedly decidi
 ng what to do next\, using tools\, and autonomously reacting to observat
 ions. In my talk\, I will discuss the use of AI agents in life sciences 
 to develop computational methods and analyses\, and to analyze and inter
 pret data in an automated fashion. Our group's experiences utilizing AI 
 agents to create ad hoc software and tools for a single task or dataset\
 , will be covered. I will then introduce MuFM\, a foundation model for s
 omatic variants whose development process has been semi-automated and ag
 ent-driven. The talk concludes with the prospects of fully automating co
 mputational method development and data analysis for life sciences.
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
